                "content": "# KLAMATH RIVER BASIN.\n\nEXTREMES OF STAGE.--Maximum stage recorded during year, 27.0 feet at 9 a. m. Janu- ary 22 (discharge, 130,000 second-feet); minimum stage recorded, 5.9 feet Sep- tember 2 and 3 (discharge, 2,980 second-feet).\n\n1911-1914: Maximum stage recorded, 28.5 feet at 9 p. m. February 17, 1912 (discharge, 142,000 second-feet); minimum stage recorded, 5.3 feet September 23 and 24, 1911 (discharge, 2,440 second-feet).\n\nDIVERSIONS.-Water is diverted for irrigation and power development from main river and tributaries in Oregon and California. Accuracy.-Rating curve fairly well defined; results good.\n\nNo discharge measurements were made during the year.\n\nDaily discharge, in second-feet, of Klamath River near Requa, Cal., for the year ending Sept. 30, 1914.",
